step	1	-	Quick guide step 1
line	<col=000080>Talk to a <col=800000>Legends' Guard</col> east of <col=800000>Ardougne</col> . Fairy ring BLR.</col>
step	2	-	Quick guide step 2
line	<str>Talk to a Legends' Guard east of Ardougne . Fairy ring BLR.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to <col=800000>Radimus</col>. (A machete can be obtained from the <col=800000>cupboards</col> next to Radimus Erkle. Papyrus can be obtained on the table next to him.)</col>
step	3	-	Quick guide step 3
line	<str>Talk to a Legends' Guard east of Ardougne . Fairy ring BLR.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Radimus. (A machete can be obtained from the cupboards next to Radimus Erkle. Papyrus can be obtained on the table next to him.)</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Head to the Kharazi Jungle, south of Shilo Village (fairy ring CKR or gnome glider to Karamja (aka Gandius) then cross the stepping stones towards the south-west). You will need to chop through the jungle bush. (You can get papyrus and charcoal from Shilo village General store, if needed)</col>
step	4	-	Quick guide step 4
line	<str>Talk to a Legends' Guard east of Ardougne . Fairy ring BLR.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Radimus. (A machete can be obtained from the cupboards next to Radimus Erkle. Papyrus can be obtained on the table next to him.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the Kharazi Jungle, south of Shilo Village (fairy ring CKR or gnome glider to Karamja (aka Gandius) then cross the stepping stones towards the south-west). You will need to chop through the jungle bush. (You can get papyrus and charcoal from Shilo village General store, if needed)</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Note: The <col=800000>vanilla pod</col> needed for <col=800000>Recipe for Disaster/Freeing Sir Amik Varze</col> is accessible at this point. It is on the southern coast between the West and Middle sections of the jungle. Finish the mapping before leaving to save yourself a trip. You do not need to have started the subquest in order to pick the vanilla pod.</col>
step	5	-	Quick guide step 5
line	<str>Talk to a Legends' Guard east of Ardougne . Fairy ring BLR.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Radimus. (A machete can be obtained from the cupboards next to Radimus Erkle. Papyrus can be obtained on the table next to him.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the Kharazi Jungle, south of Shilo Village (fairy ring CKR or gnome glider to Karamja (aka Gandius) then cross the stepping stones towards the south-west). You will need to chop through the jungle bush. (You can get papyrus and charcoal from Shilo village General store, if needed)</str>
line	
line	<str>Note: The vanilla pod needed for Recipe for Disaster/Freeing Sir Amik Varze is accessible at this point. It is on the southern coast between the West and Middle sections of the jungle. Finish the mapping before leaving to save yourself a trip. You do not need to have started the subquest in order to pick the vanilla pod.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Start mapping on either the east or west to save having to backtrack. For each part of the jungle (west, middle, and east), right-click Radimus notes and select the 'complete' option. Make sure you successfully map a section before moving to the next.</col>
step	6	-	Quick guide step 6
line	<str>Talk to a Legends' Guard east of Ardougne . Fairy ring BLR.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Radimus. (A machete can be obtained from the cupboards next to Radimus Erkle. Papyrus can be obtained on the table next to him.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the Kharazi Jungle, south of Shilo Village (fairy ring CKR or gnome glider to Karamja (aka Gandius) then cross the stepping stones towards the south-west). You will need to chop through the jungle bush. (You can get papyrus and charcoal from Shilo village General store, if needed)</str>
line	
line	<str>Note: The vanilla pod needed for Recipe for Disaster/Freeing Sir Amik Varze is accessible at this point. It is on the southern coast between the West and Middle sections of the jungle. Finish the mapping before leaving to save yourself a trip. You do not need to have started the subquest in order to pick the vanilla pod.</str>
line	
line	<str>Start mapping on either the east or west to save having to backtrack. For each part of the jungle (west, middle, and east), right-click Radimus notes and select the 'complete' option. Make sure you successfully map a section before moving to the next.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Use the notes on a <col=800000>Jungle forester</col> south of Shilo to obtain the <col=800000>bullroarer</col>. (If they don't want it, read the map first)</col>
