line	<str>Talk to Radimus. (A machete can be obtained from the cupboards next to Radimus Erkle. Papyrus can be obtained on the table next to him.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the Kharazi Jungle, south of Shilo Village (fairy ring CKR or gnome glider to Karamja (aka Gandius) then cross the stepping stones towards the south-west). You will need to chop through the jungle bush. (You can get papyrus and charcoal from Shilo village General store, if needed)</str>
line	
line	<str>Note: The vanilla pod needed for Recipe for Disaster/Freeing Sir Amik Varze is accessible at this point. It is on the southern coast between the West and Middle sections of the jungle. Finish the mapping before leaving to save yourself a trip. You do not need to have started the subquest in order to pick the vanilla pod.</str>
line	
line	<str>Start mapping on either the east or west to save having to backtrack. For each part of the jungle (west, middle, and east), right-click Radimus notes and select the 'complete' option. Make sure you successfully map a section before moving to the next.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the notes on a Jungle forester south of Shilo to obtain the bullroarer. (If they don't want it, read the map first)</str>
line	
line	<str>Cut your way back into the Kharazi Jungle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Swing the bullroarer by a totem pole to summon Gujuo (if it doesn't work, try another totem pole).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Gujuo.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the Mossy rock at the north-western section of the jungle and crawl inside. (50 Agility required)</str>
line	
line	<str>Investigate the Fire Wall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the cave and use the bullroarer again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use 2 gold bars on an anvil (barbarian anvils do not work) with a hammer to smith a golden bowl. You can fail this. You no longer need a hammer nor the sketch after this step.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bullroarer in Kharazi Jungle and have Gujuo enchant the bowl.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Water Pool (west of the centre of the jungle), use your machete on the nearby reeds, and use the reeds on the pool.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the cave to the north-west again and search the eastern bookcase to squeeze through the crevice behind it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your lockpick on the gate, then smash the three boulders (failing to smash a boulder can reduce your Mining level by 1, bring a restore potion if needed).</str>
line	
line	<str>Push open the next gate (requires 50 Strength) then walk south-west then north-west until you reach a marked wall, jumping over the jagged walls on the way. (Kill a death wing for the Hard Karamja Diary if needed)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the marked wall. If you fail to do this first, your runes will be consumed and you'll need more.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your runes on the marked wall in order (Soul, Mind, Earth, Law, Law).</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the cut gems on the carved rocks (not the ore rocks). Use the map on the right to see which gem goes where.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the binding book and read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport out to prepare for the fight against Nezikchened, and return to the first room of the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Refill your bowl with sacred water, if needed. (Leaving the jungle has a chance to evaporate the water.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the golden bowl (be sure it is filled with sacred water) on the fire surrounding Ungadulu.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the binding book on Ungadulu (careful not to left-click attack him).</str>
line	
line	<str>Defeat Nezikchened. (Lvl-187).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ungadulu (careful not to left-click attack).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit, then summon and speak with Gujuo.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your bowl of water on the seeds.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cut some more reeds and attempt to refill the bowl.</str>
line	
line	<str>Call and talk with Gujuo.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using the map above, collect the ardrigal (search the large-leaved palm trees) and snake weed (search one of the marshy jungle vines) if extra were not obtained during Jungle Potion. Mix them with a vial of water for a bravery potion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Drink the potion now to save space. Prepare to go through the cave again. You do not need the SMELL runes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the cave to the chamber with the gem-pools where you found the binding book. Cast the charge orb spell on the north gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your rope on the winch and climb down. Drink the bravery potion first if you haven't already</str>
line	
line	<str>Do not interact with the blue hat if you wish to choose the "good" path.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the rocks to reach the bottom. You can again fall and take a lot of damage (40+).</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill each of the 3 different skeletons (Lvl-106, Lvl-100, and Lvl-92) to get the 3 crystal pieces.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use each crystal piece on the north-east furnace.</str>
line	
line	<str>There is 1 searchable mossy rock in the middle of this room. Use the heart on it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run south-east and use the heart on the recess next to the barrier. Walk through the barrier.</str>
line	
line	<str>Push one of the boulders to the west and then talk to Echned Zekin.</str>
line	
line	<str>For the "evil" short path:</str>
line	
line	<str>For the "good" long path:</str>
line	
line	<str>Skills needed: 45 Herblore (boostable) Use the germinated seeds on the fertile soil patch (8 steps north and 5 steps west of the pool). Note: It is possible to be unsuccessful when planting the seeds. Plant the seeds again until a sapling grows. If more seeds are needed, visit the cave and speak to Ungadulu for more.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once planted, the yommi bush will grow leaves. Use the sacred water on it and it will become an adult yommi tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your axe on the adult yommi tree. Use your axe on the downed tree twice to make it into a totem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Lift it from the ground and you will now have a yommi totem in your inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>If "evil" path was chosen:</str>
line	
line	<str>If "good" path was chosen:</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your totem on the pole again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gujuo will appear and give you a gilded totem. If he doesn't show up, swing the bullroarer.</str>
line	
line	<str>Collect 5 palm leaves by shaking a Leafy Palm Tree near the Water Pool for the Karamja Hard Diary if needed (you can drop and pick up the same palm leaf several times).</str>
line	
line	<str>Collect a vanilla pod south-west of the Water Pool for Recipe for Disaster if needed.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Radimus at the Legends Guild (fairy ring BLR) with the gilded totem AND Radimus notes.</col>
